# Save context

Write the current task document or a snapshot at the user's path. Record task ID, repository, worktree, branch, base ref and commit, status, changed files, decisions with their sources, permissions actually granted, executed checks with commands and revision, failures, open questions, and next concrete actions. Link large logs rather than copying them. Use the existing state-root and slug tools. Do not commit a private snapshot unless requested. Confirm the file can be read back before reporting it saved.
